# Ask when the user can do it better

When a step is easy for the user and makes the result safer, faster, or easier to edit, ask them to do that step before doing it yourself.

This includes creating or placing Unity objects, saving a selection as a connected prefab, and wiring a serialized reference in the Inspector.

Keep going on the code and data that are safer for you to change. After they reply, use what they created instead of generating it.

```text
This button needs a scene object and a serialized reference on ShopScreen.
Creating the button and assigning it in the Inspector keeps the file IDs valid.
I can then read that reference from ShopScreen. Want to set that up before I change the script?
```
